            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The choice of paleoclimate explanatory variables, i.e. air surface temperature (\u00b0C) and precipitation (m/year), was a compromise between the ecological relevance of environmental variables for sturgeons and the availability in paleoclimate model outputs. Annual air surface temperature was used as a proxy of water temperature in the catchments, as the latter was not available at the European scale. It refers to the conditions encountered by sturgeons during spawning periods. Reconstructions of paleo-river flows only exist for a few hydrological systems while precipitation was available at the desired scale as a limiting hydrological factor representing the hydraulic potential of the catchment (Lassalle et al., 2009). The downscaled paleoclimate model outputs from the intermediate complexity coupled climate model iLOVECLIM (Arthur et al., 2023, 2022) were chosen because they fitted the study coverage/area (i.e. Europe) and study timeframe (11,500-100 years BP).",
